    type. Bytes are written in and retrieved exactly as given, but it will
    raise TypeErrors if something other than bytes are written.

    Example::

        >>> from boltons import ioutils
        >>> with ioutils.SpooledBytesIO() as f:
        ...     f.write(b"Happy IO")
        ...     _ = f.seek(0)
